      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The proliferation of Pacinian corpuscles is a rare benign lesion that occurs frequently in the fingers of hands, with the only clinical sign of pain when a drastic temperature change happens. A case of an extremely rare lesion in which we observed hypertrophy and hyperplasia of Pacinian corpuscles has been reported."},
